    {
      "id": "claim_11e6049b6f774dc6ad10ede98b1cb9a6",
      "statement": "`Catalog.include`/`exclude`/`wrap` are fluent policies keyed by DTO class name or the name as a string: `include` and `exclude` assign (replace) rather than accumulate — so `include()` with no arguments publishes nothing — while `wrap` stores one wrapper per DTO name and a later `wrap` for the same name overwrites the earlier one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/catalog.py#L103-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4ef8367808159eafd390b9300f07870e75a5dedca91840dd8324abb7cf752481:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/catalog.py#L57-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:623829ab0779305f6969d5a45737ed6cdb620ff3a85fd4e41ea15a4e290a07b3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7637812cfd8b498eadef461ea29c31a9",
      "statement": "`get_scalar_use_cases(filter_binaries_schema=False)` is the single entry point both hosts call: it projects features then application services (that order) and, when the flag is true, keeps only entries satisfying `json_utils.is_binary_free(entry.json_schema, entry.dto)`, logging `Skipping non-JSON Feature/ApplicationService [%s]` for each drop. The default is permissive, and both MCP (`server()`) and JSON-RPC (`index_methods`) explicitly pass `filter_binaries_schema=True`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/catalog.py#L116-L156",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e61044a76b425d0fe25c897a6d673cf44ae5de0e9f709f668dcf417dcd0e703:"
        },
        {
