    {
      "id": "claim_f8d5a1afd8004d7cbcb28489b0a51735",
      "statement": "`json_utils` answers whether a DTO can travel as JSON with two independent checks: a full recursive walk of the pydantic JSON Schema tree (`properties`, `$defs`/`definitions`, `items`, `additionalProperties`, `anyOf`/`oneOf`/`allOf`, with a `seen` set of node ids so cyclic `$defs` terminate) looking for `format` in `BINARY_JSON_FORMATS = {\"binary\", \"byte\"}`, plus a check of the DTO's own field annotations against `BINARY_TYPES = (bytes, bytearray, memoryview)` that recurses through generics so `list[bytes]` or `bytes | None` is caught.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/const.py#L16-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6474bc72114ed613dfc93e69b5741f1637782a25c7ff32377ad02c4ca40bad43:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/json_utils.py#L1-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:671409024d194a9b7d434b65a3a37894f250ebe6c46c99cb0a6ee3b9979d47ed:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/json_utils.py#L26-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a872b143352e520b5639bca8725000aead2a8a4c64339643e9a8395a8de8631:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9439646304d64a4cae4c43dc2f707761",
      "statement": "The three `json_utils` entry points differ deliberately: `dto_json_schema` degrades to `{\"type\": \"object\", \"title\": dto_type.__name__}` on any exception so the catalog stays total, `is_binary_free` takes an already-built schema and the DTO class so the catalog can avoid building the schema twice, and `dto_is_json_serializable` fails closed because it builds the schema itself.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/catalog.py#L152-L152",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9916214c8a579c76cafd47970fb4a7d08d87e5f4e7105cb33d4a57fd4b4f6f67:"
        },
        {
