    {
      "id": "claim_6591200ee07348a781690efeb59d8653",
      "statement": "`scalar_executor.execute(framework_instance, run, payload, context=None)` is the optional context/tracing layer over a bound `run`: it pops `TRACE_KEYS = (\"trace_id\", \"span_id\", \"carrier\")` out of the context into `trace_kwargs` and enters `framework.context(extra)` and/or `framework.with_trace(**trace_kwargs)` only when each has content, nesting the context block outside the trace block. JSON-RPC uses it because `context` is a sibling member of its request; the MCP host does not need it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/entrypoint_rpc.md#L161-L161",
