    {
      "id": "claim_0c04caf89b9a4326bf4d99f7485660bb",
      "statement": "A new host is meant to reuse this layer rather than reimplement it: it adds a `{protocol}.py` holding only wire-specific code, a thin `entrypoint.py` facade that builds a `Catalog` and maps `get_scalar_use_cases(filter_binaries_schema=True)` onto the wire, and an optional extra for its own library, imported lazily inside the method that needs it and raised as a named `ImportError` chained from the original one.",
